# `cell init` refuses a plan as lost when a wipe leaves exactly a Phase-2
# quorum of its members intact: the cell looks lost when it is not (#909
# (oracles that do not judge)). The verdict from ground truth
# (`tail::judge_lost`) does not see a lost cell here, so the tail checks
# and the `cell init` oracles must catch the refusal.
expect: caught
cause: init: init is refused as cell_lost only once a majority of initial members was wiped
file: crates/lib/paros-machine/src/cell_init.rs
--- find
    if intact.len() < q2 {
--- replace
    if intact.len() < q2 || (intact.len() == q2 && intact.len() < plan.members.len()) {
--- end
